// Dialogue testbed — the map tapes/interact_prompt.tape and
// tapes/dialogue_branch.tape run against.
//
// A long empty room with a step down into a two-tile bay at the far end, and
// Runa the Herbalist in the bay. Deliberately empty otherwise: the tapes here
// are about a conversation, and every hazard, knight or moving platform in the
// room would be one more thing the run's timing depended on.
//
// A new file rather than an addition to testbed_arena.ron, which is frozen —
// its tapes encode its exact pixels. Treat this one as a fixture too: add to
// it, but do not move what is already here.
//
// **Why the bay exists.** A villager has `Patrol` and no `Hostile`, so it
// paces, and a patroller only ever turns at a wall or at the edge of what it is
// standing on — which means its route is as wide as the room it is in. Runa
// crossing four hundred pixels while the player walks over would make every
// assertion in both tapes depend on when, exactly, she turned round. The step
// pens her into a thirty-pixel beat she cannot stroll out of, the player walks
// off the ledge into the bay and is stopped by the far wall, and the two are
// then within reach of each other for as long as either tape cares to take.
// Neither tape times anything: run right until the wall stops you, and she is
// there.
//
// The villager has no grid character, and that is the same call `Platform` and
// `Swing` are under. `K` exists because a knight is the same wherever you drop
// one; a talking NPC is not — it carries a conversation, and which conversation
// is the whole of what distinguishes one from another. So it is an
// `Npc(kind:, cell:)` entry, and what it says comes from its stat block's
// `interact:` group in assets/data/stats.ron.
//
// Legend: '#' solid  'P' spawn.
//
// 18x10 tiles at 32px = 576x320 world pixels.
//
//   spawn        col 2,  row 6    world (70, 190), feet on the ledge at y=224
//   upper floor  row 7, cols 0-14 surface y=224, x 0..480
//   bay          cols 15-16       floor surface y=256, x 480..544
//   right wall   col 17           interior edge x=544
//   villager     col 15, row 7    world (485, 226), box 485..507
//
// Runa strolls at 24 px/s. She turns back at the step when her leading edge
// plus a 6px look-ahead reaches x=480, and at the far wall when it reaches
// x=544, so she paces x 485..516 and never leaves the bay. The player runs the
// 410px from the spawn, walks off the ledge at x=480, drops the one tile into
// the bay and is stopped by the wall at x=524 — inside the 24px interact reach
// of her whole beat. Getting out again is a jump, which is what the "walk away
// and the prompt clears" half of interact_prompt.tape does.
Level(
    tileset: "castle",
    grid: [
        "##################",
        "#................#",
        "#................#",
        "#................#",
        "#................#",
        "#................#",
        "#.P..............#",
        "###############..#",
        "##################",
        "##################",
    ],
    entities: [
        Npc(kind: "villager", cell: (15, 7)),
    ],
)
